# Ranch Node Tailworm Audit — Tailscale TS-2026-014 → TS-2026-017

**Audit date:** Tuesday 2026-11-10, ~20:10–20:25 CST (America/Chicago)
**Scope:** Will Bickford's ranch fleet (the "shell of nine," now 25 nodes) + awsbox.
**Method:** read-only, per node — Tailscale version, Tailscale SSH state, `tailscale serve` configuration, OpenSSH service state. Nothing was changed on any node. No credentials, keys, or secrets are recorded here.
**Task coordinate:** 22.8.12/10.8.15/5.6.7

## What Tailworm is

On 2026-10-25, Cyberdione Labs published "Tailworm," an 11-finding audit of the Tailscale client (tested on 1.104.2) and the headscale control server (tested on 0.29.5). Tailscale confirmed the client-side issues in four security bulletins dated 2026-10-26 and shipped the fixes in client **1.104.4 on 2026-10-28**:

| Bulletin | Surface | Flaw |
|---|---|---|
| TS-2026-014 (High) | Tailscale SSH | Unix-socket forwarding ran as **root** inside tailscaled, with a path-allowlist race — a peer allowed to SSH in could reach root-only sockets (Docker socket, the tailscaled local API) and escalate to root. Wormable in lab tests at under a second per hop. |
| TS-2026-015 | Tailscale SSH | Unbounded session memory retention — repeated window/env messages grew tailscaled by ~536 MB in 7 s and it stayed high after disconnect (denial of service). |
| TS-2026-016 | `tailscale serve` | Unguarded `serve --tcp` / Unix-socket backends could reach privileged sockets, including the tailscaled local API. |
| TS-2026-017 | `tailscale serve` | HTTP/2 shared-context race bled `Tailscale-App-Capabilities` headers across mounts. |

Key facts for judging exposure:

- **All four are fixed in 1.104.4 or later.** Any client older than 1.104.4 is treated as unpatched.
- TS-2026-014/015 apply only to nodes **running Tailscale SSH**. Standard OpenSSH reached over the tailnet is **not** affected.
- TS-2026-016/017 apply only to nodes **running `tailscale serve`**.
- An attacker must already hold a tailnet foothold — a device the policy already allows to SSH in. This is privilege escalation, not an internet-facing break-in. No exploitation in the wild has been reported by Tailscale or the researchers; no CVEs assigned.
- Interim stopgap for a node that cannot be updated: set `TS_SSH_DISABLE_FORWARDING=1` in the tailscaled environment and restart the service.

## Verdict summary

**No exposed nodes found.** All 14 nodes assessed are running **Tailscale 1.104.5** (one patch release past the 1.104.4 fix) with Tailscale SSH **not enabled** — the fleet logs in through ordinary OpenSSH over the tailnet, which Tailworm does not touch. Two assessed nodes run `tailscale serve` on the patched client. Eleven tailnet devices could not be fully assessed and are listed as **unassessed**, never cleared — though the seven online ones advertise no Tailscale SSH and no Serve services to the tailnet.

## Assessed nodes (14)

Every node below: version **1.104.5**, Tailscale SSH **off**, OpenSSH active (the fleet's actual login path — not a Tailworm surface).

| Node | Tailscale | TS SSH | Serve | Verdict |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| aletheia-core | 1.104.5 | off | none configured | **Current** |
| Rock Mountain | 1.104.5 | off | none configured | **Current** |
| Scroll Central | 1.104.5 | off | none configured | **Current** |
| Quacked Hill | 1.104.5 | off | HTTPS site, tailnet-only, proxying to a localhost app on port 4318 (HTTP backend, no Unix-socket backend) | **Current** — serve surface present, patched client |
| Orchid Flow | 1.104.5 | off | none configured | **Current** |
| Plain View | 1.104.5 | off | none configured | **Current** |
| Ni Knight | 1.104.5 | off | none configured | **Current** |
| Ashfall Haven | 1.104.5 | off | none configured | **Current** |
| Elven Path | 1.104.5 | off | HTTPS site, tailnet-only, serving local files and a localhost proxy | **Current** — serve surface present, patched client |
| Free Fall | 1.104.5 | off | none configured | **Current** |
| Halycon Vector | 1.104.5 | off | none configured | **Current** |
| Lighthouse Omen | 1.104.5 | off | none configured | **Current** |
| Logos Prime | 1.104.5 | off | none configured | **Current** |
| awsbox | 1.104.5 | off | none configured | **Current** |

Notes:

- Quacked Hill's and Elven Path's Serve sites are **tailnet-only** (not Funnel/public) and use HTTP/file backends — neither uses the Unix-socket backend pattern behind TS-2026-016 — and both run the patched 1.104.5 client regardless.
- No node anywhere in the fleet was found running Tailscale SSH, so the root-escalation bulletin (TS-2026-014) has no live surface here even before the version check.

## Unassessed nodes (11) — not cleared

These devices are on the tailnet but could not be logged into during this audit, so their client versions are **unknown**. They are listed here rather than marked safe.

**Online, partial signal (7):** kaleidoscope-one, yeet-max, jacked-kite, great-white, moon-beam, west-lincoln, uncanny-valley.
- Not in the ranch access configuration, so no login was attempted. From the tailnet's own peer data, all seven currently advertise **no Tailscale SSH host keys and no Serve services** — encouraging, but their client versions are unverified.
- Uncanny Valley is a special case: it is operated on-prem by another person (SSH account is not Will's), and access has been awaiting a key grant since 2026-11-05.

**Offline at audit time (4):** aurora-continuum, delta-wood, best-willow, splinter. (Aurora Continuum, Delta Wood, and Best Willow have been unreachable since 2026-11-04.) An offline node cannot be attacked over the tailnet, but it also cannot be verified — each should be checked when it next comes online, before it is trusted.

**Not audited (out of scope):** the non-Linux tailnet devices — Will's phone (Orin, Android), lilly (Windows), Dylan's Mac mini (macOS). Tailworm's confirmed bulletins concern the Linux client surfaces above; if a full-fleet sweep is wanted, these can be added.

## Staged upgrade commands (prepared, NOT run)

No assessed node needs one — all are already past 1.104.4. For any unassessed node that later turns out to be below 1.104.4, the staged commands are:

```sh
# Preferred — Tailscale's own updater:
sudo tailscale update

# Equivalent via the system package manager (all ranch nodes are apt-based):
sudo apt-get update && sudo apt-get install -y tailscale

# Verify afterwards:
tailscale version    # must report 1.104.4 or later

# Interim stopgap only, if a node cannot be updated yet (TS-2026-014):
# add TS_SSH_DISABLE_FORWARDING=1 to the tailscaled service environment
# (e.g. /etc/default/tailscaled) and restart tailscaled.
```

Per the audit's terms, these are staged for Will's approval — **no upgrade was applied to any node during this audit.**

## Bottom line

The fleet is current: 14 of 14 assessed nodes on 1.104.5, Tailscale SSH off everywhere, Serve present on two nodes and patched on both. The remaining work is not patching — it is closing the visibility gap on the 11 unassessed devices, seven of which are online right now but outside the ranch access configuration.
